# Documentation Rules

Before starting work in a new session, read in this order:
1. `memory.md`
2. `scope.md`
3. `architecture.md`
4. `design.md`
5. `DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`
6. `plan.md`
7. `tasks.md`

After completing meaningful work:
- Update `tasks.md` (check off completed items; add newly discovered ones).
- Update `memory.md` — append a dated Session Log entry (Decision / Architecture / Design / Completed / Next / Notes format already used in the file). Keep it compact; never paste full conversation transcripts.
- Document any new or changed architectural decision inline in `architecture.md` or `DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` (whichever it belongs to), not only in `memory.md`.
- Do not rewrite historical `memory.md` entries unless a decision was actually reversed — if reversed, add a new entry noting the change and why; don't silently delete the old one.

The repository documentation (`memory.md`, `scope.md`, `architecture.md`, `design.md`, `DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`) is the source of truth for the project. A new session must never require prior chat history to understand current state.
